# idle-plug: whose idle bodies end an order. Four corridors 8 cells wide, each plugged wall to wall by four idle
# bodies that were never ordered; six bodies of player 0 are sent through each to a point beyond it.
#   A  the player's own idle bodies in the way, a move order
#   B  an ally's idle bodies (player 1, same team), a move order
#   C  an enemy's idle bodies (player 2), a move order
#   D  the player's own idle bodies, an attack-move order
# Idle bodies packed from wall to wall have no cell to part to, and no rule moves them: A, B and D stood before
# their plug for good with their orders. They now end them there (the stand-down, 600 dead ticks against bodies
# that will never move): an ally's body counts as the player's own. C keeps its orders: an enemy's body is never a
# reason to end one (Legion moves no enemy body; Retail ends C as well).
# Keys: g.A.complete_n, g.B.complete_n, g.D.complete_n (6 each; 0 before), g.C.complete_n (0).
scn 1
name idle-plug
ticks 4000
seed 7
players 3
team 0 0
team 1 0
team 2 1
weapons off
map flat 128 120
wall 34 0 60 16
wall 34 24 60 16
wall 34 48 60 8
wall 34 64 60 16
wall 34 88 60 32
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
group PO 0 m 4 cells 61,17 61,19 61,21 61,23
group PY 1 m 4 cells 61,41 61,43 61,45 61,47
group PE 2 m 4 cells 61,57 61,59 61,61 61,63
group PF 0 m 4 cells 61,81 61,83 61,85 61,87
group A 0 m 6 rect 4 14 12 26 pitch=3
group B 0 m 6 rect 4 38 12 50 pitch=3
group C 0 m 6 rect 4 54 12 66 pitch=3
group D 0 m 6 rect 4 78 12 90 pitch=3
at 2 move A 112 20
at 2 move B 112 44
at 2 move C 112 60
at 2 fight D 112 84
